yeti218@hotmail.com (Yeti Pino) wrote:

> When you are blind how can you read a scroll of gold detection? I don't
> think I have ever tried this as it seems impossible to me.

You can "read" scrolls by pronouncing the formula on them. 
Shopkeepers (selling and buying), scrolls/thrones of identify, and
blessed potions of object detection will tell you what the scroll is. 
So long as you have more information than "a scroll" (i.e. "a scroll
labeled FOO", "a scroll of bar") it is enough for you to be able to
chant the formula (from memory, presumably) and use the magic
contained in the scroll.

I can see how it works, but it seems like a stretch.  Spellbooks on
the other hand are impossible to read while blind.  Of course, you
have to spend time reading them and re-read them eventually anyway, so
I think this makes some sense.

